{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-9710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ k & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $18.$ Find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-9710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ k & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ k & 0\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-24)-2(0-4k)+3(0-k) \\\\  & =8k-3k-24 \\\\  & =5k-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-18) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5k-24}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5k-24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=18$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18}{5k-24} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5k-24} & =1 \\\\ 1 & =5k-24 \\\\ 25 & =5k \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-9710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5bcc711083315f5414ee17801bf085412f4e81564c002496133c9b367a66df"} {"question" "q-9710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-9710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-9710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =5|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(0-2)+0+3(-2+3) \\\\  & =-10+0+3 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-15-0 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}=\\frac{1}{-7}\\cdot (-15)=\\frac{15}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5bcc711083315f5414ee17801bf085412f4e81564c002496133c9b367a66df"} {"question" "q-18280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-15"] ["math" "-\\frac{15}{7}"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{15}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+9)-4(0-6)+1(0+2) \\\\  & =18+24+2 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-6) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{44}\\cdot 6=\\frac{3}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18281" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5bcc711083315f5414ee17801bf085412f4e81564c002496133c9b367a66df"} {"question" "q-18281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{44}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{22}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{40}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{44}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-18281" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{22}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-1\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-1+2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-1}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{k-1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k-1 & =-2 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce5bcc711083315f5414ee17801bf085412f4e81564c002496133c9b367a66df"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=-2k-3.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2k-3\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1+2) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2k-3)}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\,2k+3\\,} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 12 & =2k+3 \\\\ 2k & =9 \\\\ k & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979275/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ac90fe3750b96429126ac1f1b005264418d78f455fcf317f27492d91657e6ba"} {"question" "q-319442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1